{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics","id":1123877,"title":"How do the various pantheons influence modern politics?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-02T08:11:34-07:00","id":1123877,"title":"How do the various pantheons influence modern politics?","content":"I was curious as to how the various pantheons influence modern politics. How exactly would they manipulate the political system in ares where they have interest? Is it subtle like through dreams or omens? Or do they get directly involved using their incarnations? Or would they influence the system through cult members, allied legendary creatures, or by way of the the inspiring bar meeting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T08:24:31-07:00","id":1123880,"title":"","content":"In 1E, where they retreated from the mortal world, I would think they act in secret.<br /> <br /> But in 2E, where the gods remained with us, it's hard to say how they might act. In fact, it's hard to say if the political system as it is today would even still exist in 2E, since many of the political changes that have occurred over the last several thousand years blatantly oppose the philosophies and traditions of the old pantheons. Mythology tells us that when mortals collectively decide to reject the gods, their city gets blown up, drowned, infested with disease, or any other variety of magical WMD's.<br /> <br /> <br /> Zeus, for example, probably wouldn't care about women's rights. Hell, he doesn't even respect actual goddesses, so the idea of him respecting a mortal woman is flat out absurd. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And nobody can sit there and tell me that the gods would change with the times like mortals do, because A) Most of the gods consider mortals to be beneath them, and B) they can hold grudges against those who wronged them for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> The Gods do not simply let things go...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-02-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T08:30:29-07:00","id":1123883,"title":"","content":"We've had eight page long derails about whether or not the gods can change with the times or not. I'd prefer to not go through that again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T08:36:17-07:00","id":1123887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1123883#post1123883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've had eight page long derails about whether or not the gods can change with the times or not. I'd prefer to not go through that again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, right. Which topic was that one, again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T08:40:58-07:00","id":1123889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1123887#post1123887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, right. Which topic was that one, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall, but it had a lot of shoddy arguments for dragging oppression onto the center stage of the game and it made a pretty dear friend of mine quit the forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T09:13:14-07:00","id":1123898,"title":"","content":"nothing said thus far about the World indicates that anything said thus far in this thread is remotely true. I would be careful about drawing conclusions like that.<br /> <br /> I think I would try to critically examine what's been said about the World thus far and think about it in terms of genre. It does not sound like, by default, the World is so different from ours. In fact, it sounds fairly similar.<br /> <br /> So given that, you might ask yourself &quot;why have they not really meddled in politics?&quot; And you can come up with a few potential answers:<br /> <br /> 1. They don't care. I'm sure this actually covers the attitudes of many Gods, they don't really care about the structure of human government. They have other things to care about.<br /> <br /> 2. They prevent one another from meddling. There are multiple Pantheons with various visions of the world. It might be agreed upon that they don't get involved in unimportant things, because they'd rather not start an arms race based on who can meddle the most. I'm skeptical of this idea on the whole, but could imagine it to be partly true.<br /> <br /> 3. They have interfered, and the results are largely the same. Maybe power plants are bigger than they would be in our world because Hestia pushed legislation to ensure her cult would always get shrines in them, that sort of thing. This is a fun world-building opportunity, but it's worth thinking carefully about what gets added, rather than assuming they run roughshod over things.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, I could imagine the 'truth' in the World is some combination of these three things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:36:40-07:00","id":1123920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1123898#post1123898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nothing said thus far about the World indicates that anything said thus far in this thread is remotely true. I would be careful about drawing conclusions like that.<br /> <br /> I think I would try to critically examine what's been said about the World thus far and think about it in terms of genre. It does not sound like, by default, the World is so different from ours. In fact, it sounds fairly similar.<br /> <br /> So given that, you might ask yourself &quot;why have they not really meddled in politics?&quot; And you can come up with a few potential answers:<br /> <br /> 1. They don't care. I'm sure this actually covers the attitudes of many Gods, they don't really care about the structure of human government. They have other things to care about.<br /> <br /> 2. They prevent one another from meddling. There are multiple Pantheons with various visions of the world. It might be agreed upon that they don't get involved in unimportant things, because they'd rather not start an arms race based on who can meddle the most. I'm skeptical of this idea on the whole, but could imagine it to be partly true.<br /> <br /> 3. They have interfered, and the results are largely the same. Maybe power plants are bigger than they would be in our world because Hestia pushed legislation to ensure her cult would always get shrines in them, that sort of thing. This is a fun world-building opportunity, but it's worth thinking carefully about what gets added, rather than assuming they run roughshod over things.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, I could imagine the 'truth' in the World is some combination of these three things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given the level of how popular home brewing content is and the use of shard settings, I suppose it ultimately falls to the ST to decide how the World works.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think that while change is possible, it would most likely come from the Scions, rather than the old world pantheons. There are many stories in mythology that involve children overthrowing their tyrannical parents and establishing their own rule. And a story that focuses on the Scion players rising up to replace key members of their pantheon has potential to be a great story with an epic climax if done correctly.<br /> <br /> In 1E, one of the pre-made Scions tried to flaunt the expectations of Olympus by wearing modern day clothing and abiding by modern day behavior, and the book made it clear that he was not very popular because of it. To my knowledge, he wasn't outright punished for his actions, but he wasn't respected for them, either. In fact, the old gods openly mocked him about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-02-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:54:48-07:00","id":1123933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1123920#post1123920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1E, one of the pre-made Scions tried to flaunt the expectations of Olympus by wearing modern day clothing and abiding by modern day behavior, and the book made it clear that he was not very popular because of it. To my knowledge, he wasn't outright punished for his actions, but he wasn't respected for them, either. In fact, the old gods openly mocked him about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bActually it was the other way around. Donnie started wearing modern clothes on Olympus and started something of a fad for other Greek Scions to follow his lead. The books say that Greek Scions who insisted on wearing traditional Greek clothing were mocked and derided by Donnie and his clique as being a bunch of &quot;suck-ups.&quot; Donnie may have taken some heat from the Theoi themselves for a bit, but it didn't seem like it was a big deal with them. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T11:07:37-07:00","id":1123943,"title":"","content":"Whether and how the gods adapt to the modern World is a legitimate topic for discussion on the forums.<br /> <br /> There's not one single answer, and there won't be. The gods are all different people, as you'll see in the books. Most of them at least have to <i>cope</i> with it to some degree. Some gods are going to wish mortals would just go back to doing things the traditional way, with homespun clothing and tending their own flocks. Others are going to go &quot;holy shit, <i>The Walking Dead</i> is the best thing I've ever seen.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:45:51-07:00","id":1124011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1123933#post1123933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bActually it was the other way around. Donnie started wearing modern clothes on Olympus and started something of a fad for other Greek Scions to follow his lead. The books say that Greek Scions who insisted on wearing traditional Greek clothing were mocked and derided by Donnie and his clique as being a bunch of &quot;suck-ups.&quot; Donnie may have taken some heat from the Theoi themselves for a bit, but it didn't seem like it was a big deal with them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's not in the version of <b>Scion: God</b> that I've read. I'm looking at his character write up right now and it says that because Donnie tried to shun the old traditions, he lost the public's respect and was delegated to a mere errand boy after becoming a god, and the old gods know that he hates his divine name (Adonis Rhodos) but they continue to use it frequently in his presence just to annoy him. Lastly, they pretty much interact with him only to belittle him and give him new orders, but otherwise ignore his presence.<br /> <br /> So yeah, doesn't sound like modern day, pop culture Donnie Rhodes is very well liked by his pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2017, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:52:59-07:00","id":1124017,"title":"","content":"Honestly, given the fact that ancient Gods having direct influence, or even being widely worshipped, in the modern World would completely change the World's history, culture, dominating philosophies, scientific development, and yes, politics to the point of being likely unrecognizable to our own, I'd go with 1E Scion's canon and assume that Gods and magic haven't been around in the World for millennia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:08:13-07:00","id":1124025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124017#post1124017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, given the fact that ancient Gods having direct influence, or even being widely worshipped, in the modern World would completely change the World's history, culture, dominating philosophies, scientific development, and yes, politics to the point of being likely unrecognizable to our own, I'd go with 1E Scion's canon and assume that Gods and magic haven't been around in the World for millennia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing the 1e setting is supposed to be a Shard in the Companion, if I remember right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:24:54-07:00","id":1124031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124011#post1124011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That's not in the version of <b>Scion: God</b> that I've read. I'm looking at his character write up right now and it says that because Donnie tried to shun the old traditions, he lost the public's respect and was delegated to a mere errand boy after becoming a god, and the old gods know that he hates his divine name (Adonis Rhodos) but they they continue to use it frequently in his presence just to annoy him. Lastly, they pretty much interact with him only to give belittle him and give him new orders, but otherwise ignore his presence.<br /> <br /> So yeah, doesn't sound like modern day, pop culture Donnie Rhodes is very well liked by his pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHm. Maybe there's a discrepancy between his character write-up and the chapter fic detailing the Olympian's defense against Terra? I could've sworn I read about him starting a modernist fad somewhere? <br /> <br /> \u200bEh. I haven't been able to read through God in quite a while. I could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T17:09:12-07:00","id":1124088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124017#post1124017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, given the fact that ancient Gods having direct influence, or even being widely worshipped, in the modern World would completely change the World's history, culture, dominating philosophies, scientific development, and yes, politics to the point of being likely unrecognizable to our own, I'd go with 1E Scion's canon and assume that Gods and magic haven't been around in the World for millennia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm trying to say. Mythology is filled with story of mortals trying to crawl out from under the tyrannical world views of the gods, and the gods respond by obliterating their society, or threatening to do so if they don't get back in line. The last time I checked into 2nd edition previews, the old pantheons didn't retreat from the World and have remained public throughout history.<br /> <br /> So if we want to remain truthful to mythology, we should assume that modern society is dramatically different from the world we know today.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is ultimately up to the ST, and if they want to sugar coat the old pantheons to be more child friendly, that's their call. As for me, personally? I bought Scion 1E because <b>it didn't</b> try to pull that crap.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124031#post1124031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bHm. Maybe there's a discrepancy between his character write-up and the chapter fic detailing the Olympian's defense against Terra? I could've sworn I read about him starting a modernist fad somewhere?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bEh. I haven't been able to read through God in quite a while. I could be wrong. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It mentions him trying to speak with his mother (Aphrodite) in private about his mortal father having passed away, but she's too busy cheating on Hephaestus (with Ares) to give a crap. So after delivering the news, he storms off to resume his previous duties. During the trip up Olympus, Donnie is flirted with by servants of the gods, such as Amazons and Nymphs, but the actual gods themselves treat him like shit. Ares doesn't even try to hide the fact that he's doing his mother and practically tells him to say what he came there for so he can get back to it.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-02-2017, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T17:35:30-07:00","id":1124092,"title":"","content":"Remember when I said this thread shouldn't be a repeat of the other? Let's stick to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T17:48:16-07:00","id":1124097,"title":"","content":"Gods, this makes me want to spoil the Donnie fic we got in recently <i>really</i> badly. But that really needs to be presented in its full glory. I've got a bit of a crush on 2e Donnie, ngl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:06:19-07:00","id":1124103,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">It's important to keep in mind that the gods rarely interact with people in their full glory, they spin of Incarnations like Neall said<br /> &quot;t</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">heir Callings and Fate lock them into roles and relationships and they get tired of it after a while. This is also why they spin off Incarnations - to interact with mortals while Fate is running in the background and on the meta scale, rather than binding them into a thousand dramas in microcosm.&quot; that limits the amount of change they can achieve<br /> And Neall also said Gods need humanity as mirror. their mantles change. I Think Even someone sexist Like Zeus would become aaat least little bit more nice to women with the rise of feminism among his followers</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:08:56-07:00","id":1124104,"title":"","content":"Gods can't change with their mortal flocks! ...except for Ares, who goes from a bloodthirsty savage to a stately conqueror-farmer.<br /> <br /> So maybe the gods can change and there's absolutely precedent for it after all, and efforts to the contrary are looking for an excuse to add oppressors to the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:23:28-07:00","id":1124108,"title":"","content":"It's been thousands of years. You don't live thousands of years without growing up. But not everybody grows up well. There are gods who play well with mortals and gods who don't.<br /> <br /> There are rather few gods who call down all the fires of the heavens to protest US foreign policy, but it's always possible that if Ronald Reagan had asked his priest to read Mars' will in the flights of DC's pigeons, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invasion_of_Grenada\" target=\"_blank\">US might not have invaded Grenada</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:26:04-07:00","id":1124110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124103#post1124103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">And Neall also said Gods need humanity as mirror. their mantles change. I Think Even someone sexist Like Zeus would become aaat least little bit more nice to women with the rise of feminism among his followers</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought that the gods being altered by mortal perception of them was being removed from 2E?<br /> <br /> Last time I checked, there was something about Fate and mortal perception being influenced by how the gods behave around them, instead of the other way around. If a god is a sexist tyrant, Fate would guide their development towards that and mortals will attribute them to being as such.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meaning that Zeus could be misogynistic all he wants and the worst that happens is he gets a bad public reputation. I mean, Fate has already decreed he's going to be deposed by a man, so it's not like he has anything to fear from women.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124108#post1124108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been thousands of years. You don't live thousands of years without growing up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You do if you're a god. Those old empires lasted a pretty long time and the gods showed little interest in maturing over the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:29:34-07:00","id":1124112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124110#post1124110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meaning that Zeus could be misogynistic all he wants and the worst that happens is he gets a bad public reputation. I mean, Fate has already decreed he's going to be deposed by a man, so it's not like he has anything to fear from women.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, or Zeus could have gotten smashed beyond all belief one night at his son's party, gotten a drink thrown on him by a Maenad he was chatting up with some kind of &quot;golden shower&quot; line, and spent the next three hundred years with a hangover wondering how the simple fact that he wanted his dad not to digest his family had gone so wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:33:43-07:00","id":1124113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124110#post1124110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that the gods being altered by mortal perception of them was being removed from 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works like this: when you do something shitty, people remember. They'll expect you to do something shitty in the future. When a god does something shitty, they suddenly find themselves in a lot of situations where they are expected - inclined and encouraged, even - to act exactly the same way. <br /> <br /> Zeus has a wandering eye and fights with his wife all the time, even though he loves her. Fate conspires to put a lot of women in his path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:37:58-07:00","id":1124115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics#post1123877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was curious as to how the various pantheons influence modern politics. How exactly would they manipulate the political system in ares where they have interest? Is it subtle like through dreams or omens? Or do they get directly involved using their incarnations? Or would they influence the system through cult members, allied legendary creatures, or by way of the the inspiring bar meeting?</div> </div> </div> </div>As everyone here has discussed, this sort of thing is predicated on the exact sort of world an individual Storyteller is running their games in. It's sort of a crossroads between two big choices Scion Storytellers normally make when running their games. Did the Pantheons Withdraw, and Did the Pantheons Modernize? Any combination of these, with any number if small detailed changes can make for fun games. Withdrawn Pantheons, but Modernized. Present Pantheons, but Stuck in their Ways. Or even something like breaking down the questions to specific Pantheons. Modernized Present Netjer, Withdrawn Archaic Bogovi, Present Archaic Tuatha, etc. Or even break it down on the Divine Parent level.<br /> <br /> The exact answer to any of your questions Manannansun will depend on the sort of story you, or your Storyteller wants to tell. All of them can make awesome games, explore different ideas, all sorts of fun things that will work for an individual group. There is no one definitive answer to how the Pantheons influence modern politics, or how they do it. It all depends on the individual Storyteller's worlds. Maybe people could give examples of how they run their Pantheons interacting with mortal politics in their games since there is no real definitive answer. I can talk about mine, I would love to hear how other people do it!<br /> <br /> I'll start with the Tuatha since, well, you know. It's me, what do you expect. Of course I'll talk about them. So, in my games the Tuatha normally start both Archaic, and Withdrawn. The Tuath is bound by the pact forged with The Sons of Mil, they have relinquished their rights to Ireland, and withdrawn into the Sidhe Mounds. They really are not supposed to be making incursions into the normal world. They <i>do</i>, but they're not supposed to do it. Add to that almost all of their big names are dead, the Pantheon essentially doesn't get out much. When they manage to drag the dead tribe members out of the paradisiacal afterlives, and decide to break their deal with the Sons of Mil, they will <i>totally</i> get all involved in mortal politics. They won't use dreams, or legendary creatures though. The Tuatha are a conquering Divine Tribe, holding a bit of a grudge against The Sons of Mil, and almost obsessively focused on holding Ireland as their own land. The Tuatha normally set about a reconquest of Ireland. They loose the Sidhe on the mortal populations, they come out of the mounds, and do what they do best, conquer, and deal with the details later.<br /> <br /> So, less 'influence politically,' and more 'colonization and conquest.' Technically, that is using their incarnations though! Just more 'hands on' than one may expect.<br /> <br /> The other Pantheons in my games are not as... Tuatha-y as the Tuatha, and the rest would be satisfied with manipulating the situation in various ways upon their returns to the world. Some Pantheons open with threats of destruction and apocalypse if humanity doesn't 'get back on track.' The Theoi, Anunna, and Shiunesh are big on that sort of thing. The Anunna would be really annoyed that their cities have somehow vanished. The Shiunesh would just snap and start purging cities because the Shiunesh are pretty scary, getting themselves almost instantly locked into conflict with the Yazata since they overlap heavily. The Theoi would be half-self-satisfied their cultural concepts have been carried so far across the world, but they would also be <i>freaking out</i> about all the things that looked like hubris to them. So, those three would influence the world politically through big displays of Divine Might. Plagues, famines, tidal waves, earthquakes, take your pick. The Theoi would probably loose the Furies to prove a point if they could pick out a few mortals they specifically thought particularly bad and would be good examples to the rest of mortals.<br /> <br /> Some would be totally content using cults, dreams, and various miraculously interventions. The Deva, Shen, Orisha, and Abosom influence their regions through cults, traditional religious practitioners, all that sort of thing. They never really 'left,' at most are just a bit distant. Not any more distant now than they have been at any other point, I just mean distant compared to when they were running around doing their things, shaping the world, organizing things, all that. The Abosom would be continuing their support for the local Ashanti nobility, the King of the Ashanti is important to them, sort of business as usual for them. <i>Anansi</i> would be wandering around in incarnations doing Anansi-things, maybe trying to whisper in the right ears to acomplish some things he wants. <br /> <br /> So, they would be big in the category of influencing the mortal political situation through their traditional believers, oracles, and the like. <br /> <br /> The Kami are fun since their first move is very obvious. The first thing on the agenda of the Amatsukami would be returning the Emperor of Japan to his political and religious position. That's objective number one. Possibly the deploying of Takemikazuchi to the Land of Plentiful Reeds again, or perhaps just through a big, overt display of Divine Power like withdrawing the sun or something similarly massive. After Amaterasu has gotten her descendant sorted out, things would probably continue as normal. Things are going okay for the Kami with the exception of that, so after dealing with that, things would shift to being far ... less direct I guess. The Kami are sort of obsessively exact, so I would expect they would put pressure on the Emperor to put in various political policies. I don't think they would do this to be subtle, but just because this is how they exert their will on the Land of Plentiful Reeds. Individual Kami would interact with mortals and try to sway them in various ways through their oracles, but they would likely mostly keep to their Godrealms. The Kami are not huge on hanging out with mortals with a few exceptions.<br /> <br /> That would be an opening move of 'Miracles and Incarnations,' but after that mostly just using their existing religious practitioners, and the Emperor.<br /> <br /> The Bogovi are the Bogovi and would have the official policy of 'Ignore the mortals,' and then all of them would immediately go break this policy. Probably lots of trying to start up secret cults. Not secret to hide them from other mortals, but secret to hide them from the rest of the Pantheon. The Bogovi are so much fun, I still want to make a PsP for them based around violating their Virtues or something. Got all these ideals, have so much more fun not following them.<br /> <br /> So... I guess that would be through Incarnations. Perun would probably be happy with inspiring bar meetings though, he's a fun guy. Rather nice to mortals too.<br /> <br /> The Teotl would be right back to things, trying to kick-start their cults back into existence with a sort of frantic desperation to get the system back up and running. They really don't want to have to make the world again a sixth time, it's a lot of effort. The Teotl really need their cults back up and running, so a few utterly barren harvests, a few overt displays of Divinity, something to kick things back into gear. I think you would see Incarnations to start with since the Teotl need things back up and running yesterday, so Huitz hanging out as an eagle to guide his chosen people, Tezcat wandering around as The Night Axe just so scare people since Tezcatlipoca is, you know, a bit of a dick. What you might actually see is Tezcatlipoca trying to subvert the attempts of the rest of the Pantheon in bringing back their cults as a method to end the Fifth Sun so he can have another crack at being the sun when they hit the sixth try at creation.<br /> <br /> The Netjer are sort of complicated because of the political system they backed historically. I can see them potentially trying to push for a new Pharaoh, maybe some internal jockeying for position when the cults are being revived. Like a lot of the Pantheons, in my games they normally start with getting their normal religious systems back up and running, and then slipping back away from the material. I think they would be really into modern printing methods as an aside.<br /> <br /> The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s, Haida Pantheon, is in a weird situation since there are so few trained oracles left for them, and they require very specific ritual behavior from their oracles to do their own Divine Possession thing. They would probably use Incarnations mainly to influence the world, encouraging traditional systems, trying to revitalize things, that sort of stuff. Xhuuya would probably show up somewhere and do something big and flashy since that's what he does. Might just show up in the House of Assembly or something similar during an official political gathering.<br /> <br /> The Aesir... probably are content to do their own things. I would expect a decent amount of Incarnations until their religious systems get back up and running again, and then returning to their life as usual. Hanging out, traveling the Nine Worlds, doing their thing. I can see Odin, Frigg, and Freya doing some political manipulation to steer things in a way they personally desired. Freyr would probably show up on the Sweedish Royal Family's front door to get the lay of the land, see if he likes this new dynasty. He would probably be the most direct in just suggesting things change one way or another. Might be a bit confused about the monarchy not being totally dominant.<br /> <br /> After writing all of this, I think the big thing is however the Pantheons want to interact with mortal politics is the Communication Method. Some Pantheons have their communications systems still up and running, others (a lot of them) really need to kick things into gear a bit and probably need a bit of hands-on or at least using Scions as intermediaries to get things back up and running. After they have laid the divine phone lines, they can then get back into the world and start seeing what they want to do with it! And, of course, this is just how I run it, everyone else has their own systems, and that's what I love about Scion. The game is really different from table to table, with everyone enjoying something different. It's what makes Scion such a great game in my mind, the sheer amount of variation one can have from table to table in the stories that are told. It's awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:40:23-07:00","id":1124116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124112#post1124112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, or Zeus could have gotten smashed beyond all belief one night at his son's party, gotten a drink thrown on him by a Maenad he was chatting up with some kind of &quot;golden shower&quot; line, and spent the next three hundred years with a hangover wondering how the simple fact that he wanted his dad not to digest his family had gone so wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm skeptical that a Maenad would turn down a golden shower.<br /> <br /> But like I said, I'm not opposed to the idea of change coming to the pantheons. I just prefer it to come in the form of the next generation of gods (i.e Scions).<br /> <br /> It's more believable that way. Since the other option seems more like it's trying to pull the same trick God Machine did; implementing religion without offending anybody.<br /> <br /> My head canon is that the cycle of usurpation is Fate's way of updating the pantheons throughout the ages. The Scions will cast off the outdated ways of the old pantheon and establish a new, modern approach. Then, in time, they too will become outdated and another generation will; supplant them. And so on, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-02-2017, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:49:51-07:00","id":1124117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124116#post1124116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm skeptical that a Maenad would turn down a golden shower.<br /> <br /> But like I said, I'm not opposed to the idea of change coming to the pantheons. I just prefer it to come in the form of the next generation of gods (i.e Scions).<br /> <br /> It's more believable that way. Since the other option seems more like it's trying to pull the same trick God Machine did; implementing religion without offending anybody.<br /> <br /> My head canon is that the cycle of usurpation is Fate's way of updating the pantheons throughout the ages. The Scions will cast off the outdated ways of the old pantheon and establish a new, modern approach. Then, in time, they too will become outdated and another generation will; supplant them. And so on, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, Nyrufa, like I've said; the gods can and <i>have</i> changed historically. For all you talk about the Theoi being set in their ways, some of them are already noticeably different in their Roman guises, some of them quite drastically! The gods are <i>alive</i>, and just as dynamic as any mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:54:10-07:00","id":1124119,"title":"","content":"Everyone can run their games how they want, the variance is what makes Scion a really fun game! Gods can change, they stagnate, they can be present, withdrawn, on an individual level, on a Pan-Pantheon level. It's cool, people can play the game how they want to, there is no right way to play. It's whatever an individual Storyteller or Game Table wants. And, we have strayed a bit from the conversation about the influencing of Politics, I think Manannansun's question was about the method, not the function, it's a neat question. I'd love to know what people do at their tables in this regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:56:49-07:00","id":1124121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124116#post1124116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm skeptical that a Maenad would turn down a golden shower.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is <i>anybody</i> who is super-particular about their own kinks and has a FetLife profile full of &quot;and don't even message me if&quot; bullet points, it's a Maenad. They do not take shit from anyone. Except potentially as a side effect of eviscerating them.<br /> <br /> For the record, I don't mix it up with Maenads. I admire their fierceness and devotion to non-assimilation, but I can't condone the normalization of involuntary dismemberment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124116#post1124116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the other option seems more like it's trying to pull the same trick God Machine did; implementing religion without offending anybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine isn't about religion, particularly. The God-Machine is the military-industrial complex, the patriarchy, the system we are born into without our consent. It might have a nuclear plant under the Vatican, but it's also got kinetic collectors installed along the entire interstate highway system and has figured out how to run a small factory off of the tears of neglected children in a hopelessly racist and underfunded foster care system.<br /> <br /> But now that you mention it, I really am surprised that basic thesis didn't offend more people.<br /> <br /> (And if you want to talk about this further, we can do it in the CofD forums. This is Neall's show.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-02-2017, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T19:04:51-07:00","id":1124123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124121#post1124121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there is <i>anybody</i> who is super-particular about their own kinks and has a FetLife profile full of &quot;and don't even message me if&quot; bullet points, it's a Maenad. They do not take shit from anyone. Except potentially as a side effect of eviscerating them.<br /> <br /> For the record, I don't mix it up with Maenads. I admire their fierceness and devotion to non-assimilation, but I can't condone the normalization of involuntary dismemberment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The God-Machine isn't about religion, particularly. The God-Machine is the military-industrial complex, the patriarchy, the system we are born into without our consent. It might have a nuclear plant under the Vatican, but it's also got kinetic collectors installed along the entire interstate highway system and has figured out how to run a small factory off of the tears of neglected children in a hopelessly racist and underfunded foster care system.<br /> <br /> But now that you mention it, I really am surprised that basic thesis didn't offend more people. <br /> <br /> (And if you want to talk about this further, we can do it in the CofD forums. This is Neall's show.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Id be fascinated if you told me about the god machine in the demon forums Rose, I always like to hear what creators think of their characters especially their villains","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T19:07:59-07:00","id":1124124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124113#post1124113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It works like this: when you do something shitty, people remember. They'll expect you to do something shitty in the future. When a god does something shitty, they suddenly find themselves in a lot of situations where they are expected - inclined and encouraged, even - to act exactly the same way.<br /> <br /> Zeus has a wandering eye and fights with his wife all the time, even though he loves her. Fate conspires to put a lot of women in his path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I imagine fate being like a stadium full of drunken Bros yelling &quot;Cheat on her! heck yeah&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T19:40:48-07:00","id":1124141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124117#post1124117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, Nyrufa, like I've said; the gods can and <i>have</i> changed historically. For all you talk about the Theoi being set in their ways, some of them are already noticeably different in their Roman guises, some of them quite drastically! The gods are <i>alive</i>, and just as dynamic as any mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As I understand it, the Greeks and Romans had entirely different views on who / what the gods were. They worshiped the same pantheon, but not in the same fashion. So that doesn't really hold up all that well. And this is only one pantheon in particular.<br /> <br /> When I look up information about people worldwide who still venerate the old gods, I tend to find evidence of them sticking to ancient customs and traditions, rather than embracing the modern world. These religions have been around for thousands of years, far longer than monotheism and yet they have refused to adapt to the advancements of society. Hindus still have a caste system, while bathing in a sacred (lethally toxic) river, and the Shinto still ritually burn millions of household objects every year to prevent them from becoming possessed by demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you or some other Story Teller wants to modernize the pantheons in your game, I'm not stopping you. But on a personal level, I do not see it being plausible in a world where the gods stuck around and continued to influence society. In my games, society would be completely different from the world we know today, because there is valid evidence to support it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T22:22:00-07:00","id":1124182,"title":"","content":"The Deva have rarely in myth gone about making pronouncements to the people at large... they don't even have a properly coded priest class... yes, the Brahmins exist but it's not like they have an official handbook or anything... the rituals and practices of a Brahmin in one village and another a few villages over can be wildly different, even with respect to the same God.<br /> <br /> Hinduism also has no official 'oracle' type role, no individual who channels and or interprets the will of the Gods. Hindu astrology is a thing that exists but that is less 'will of the Gods' and more 'effects of the planetary cosmic rays' and is geared more to manipulating those rays through gemstones for various benefits... it's a whole pseudo-science dedicating to telling the planets to screw themselves.<br /> <br /> Divine revelations are given to individuals, but almost exclusively to people who were looking for it in the first place... the Gods don't proselytize. People do, and there are stories of non-believing mortals being inspired by devout individuals and getting visions from Gods themselves, but the Gods don't go out of their way to convert people... they're Gods, they may enjoy the worship, but they don't need it.<br /> <br /> (This is a giant departure from Vedic era Hinduism, where the Deva are practically the Teotl in how much they need and want sacrifice and the reciprocal relationship between Gods and Man is paramount... but discussing the massive changes that religions go through and the drastic ways in which Gods change over time is out of the scope of this thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Instead, because of the above, when Deva seek to influence the world, their most common avenue is Incarnations. Quite a few historical figures are considered Incarnations of various Gods, and while this is generally done to religious figures, I don't see why a Deva couldn't Incarnate as a politician or a sports star or a world renowned musician or scientist. This has an added advantage... the Deva as Gods are often expected to be paragons, to some extent detached from the foibles and bonds of humanity... Incarnations, being human, are expected to and even encouraged to be human and have human traits, which makes their stories more interesting than 'perfect God does everything perfectly'.<br /> <br /> As a side note, because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> brought this up, the caste system is totally a thing that exists, despite the government's ban on caste based discrimination long ago... for right-hand path Hindus, who believe that the caste system is God given. Left-hand path Hindus (myself included) gave up on caste based distinctions hundreds of years ago, also citing Godly revelation. Neither side has been hit with the wrath of God yet, so the only real reason to go with one over the other is how big a bag of dicks you want the Gods to be, and while it's fine if you want the Deva to be a bag of dicks, that position has no more religious validity than the other one... not to mention the many myths where Gods themselves don't care about caste, like the one where Lakshmi abandons Vishnu over her visiting an untouchable devotee or Sarasvati Incarnating herself into a Chandala family to make a point and eventually rising to Goddesshood again as Matangi. Idols of the Supreme Mother Durga must be made with a handful of dirt from a prostitute's courtyard, and the Tantrik followers of Kali (including yours truly) deny all distinction of caste and even allow women to be priestesses and spiritual guides, which most Right-Hand traditions do not. Most Bhakti traditions following Vishnu and Shiva also do not discriminate on caste lines or discard the system altogether, though being a Shakta I'm less familiar with them, so even mythically as well as religiously there is plenty of precedent for the Deva dumping the caste sytem in the cesspit it belongs. <br /> <br /> Speaking of cesspits, most priests in (at least my corner of) India don't use Ganges water anymore. For my father's last rites, the priest just spoke the names of the seven sacred rivers over a bottle of tap water and we used that for the ceremony. This is a modern innovation to circumvent the toxic water because, you know, we're not blind and know perfectly well that the water of the actual Ganges is a death sentence (also an example of how religions innovate). Also, instead of providing the priest a cow as a gift as is traditionally required in the sacred texts (since the apartment he lives in doesn't allow pets) I handed him a hundred bucks and officially announced to the Gods that the hundred bucks should be considered a cow in their eyes. And so it was done <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Religions change and adapt with the times, they wouldn't survive otherwise.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd just like to remind people that the Deva Virtues are Duty <i>and Conscience</i> after all. And I don't know if it was intentional or not but they do correspond pretty perfectly to right hand path and left hand path Hinduism. Given the level of research evinced by Mendez' work so far, I am tending towards it being intentional <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T22:40:07-07:00","id":1124184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124182#post1124182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enlightening Things</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for clarifying. I was watching a video on most dangerous places to visit and one of them depicted people washing idols and letting their children swim in the river, so I wasn't sure if that was still a major thing or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> But on that note, I've been watching educational videos about some of this stuff and discovered that some of the old pantheons such as the Norse and Pesedjet actually did have human characteristics. Namely, their deities were subject to disease, age and physical injury. When one or more gods became unfit to do their jobs, they passed their station onto somebody more qualified. Which is how I like to imagine modernization happened over the ages in the Scion setting. Some pantheons would adapt better than others, given the nature of how their pantheons and cultures work.<br /> <br /> The Greeks, for example, are among some of the most egocentric, megalomaniac ass holes in all the mythology I've come across. If you're not a god, they don't care about your opinion. If you are a god, they don't care unless you're more popular than them. If you're more popular than them, they will challenge you in front of everybody to satisfy their insecurities. If you win said challenge, they throw a temper tantrum!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2017, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T07:01:40-07:00","id":1124283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124141#post1124141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If you or some other Story Teller wants to modernize the pantheons in your game, I'm not stopping you. But on a personal level, I do not see it being plausible in a world where the gods stuck around and continued to influence society. In my games, society would be completely different from the world we know today, because there is valid evidence to support it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is from what we know of the &quot;default&quot; setting presented via the various previews and the ask Neal thread the gods don't have the same influence they once had, even if their religions have stayed stronger and more mainstream than the real world. We know that the Orisha have both failed to prevent a massive and far reaching tragedy from hitting their people, and changed to accommodate the situation. The Teotl preview mentions aspects of Mexican culture that are at least partially imports of Spain, which implies that the mass murder, enslavement, and intermingling of culture/genetics that gave birth to modern Central American culture still happened, and this is without, to the best of my knowledge, the pantheon worshiped by the Iberians being mentioned at all in any fashion in any official Scion 2e material that\u2019s been shown to the community, so I assume there would not have been many, if any, powerful deities actively backing Cortez against the Teotl. Both of these imply to me that the gods may act as modifiers, but they probably don\u2019t want to make big moves that often. It would mostly be the details that change.<br /> <br /> I think that while many gods would be stuck in their ways others would have been more lax, or even enthusiastic, about certain changes. You only have to look at a summary of the Iliad to see that even within a single Pantheon the gods would effectively be tripping up each other\u2019s attempts to take a firm hand to humanity. Zeus might grumble about women\u2019s Lib but Artemis would have been showering the leaders with blessings. I think the influence of the gods would have especially waned between the time of the real world Renaissance and age of reason and the information age. When human population and technology would have taken off, probably aided by the artisan and crafting gods of different cultures. As more humans begin doing things faster the Gods would find it harder to, ahem, put the fear of god, into as large a percentage of the population at once, for example humans learning about medicine would make plagues slightly less terrifying, especially if there are multiple gods of healing and if you annoy one into trying to smite your city you can always sacrifice to a different one and hope they cushion the blow, something that can\u2019t really happen in standard mythology. Even with them still being active and still having believers they\u2019d likely suffer a downswing in direct cultural influence until Gods could do things like sit down during FDR\u2019s radio addresses and correct their priesthood misinterpreting their Divine will.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T07:35:39-07:00","id":1124291,"title":"","content":"That does beg the question though, if the &quot;Age of Reason&quot; would have happened to begin with? The whole concept behind it is that humanity veered away from superstition and started using science to rationalize and explain the world around them.<br /> <br /> But in a game like Scion, all that superstitious stuff is real. There are divine, nigh omnipotent beings who control the heavens and the earth. There are ghosts who linger after death, there is an underworld full of demons and departed spirits. There are actual elves, giants, centaurs and all kinds of other mythical creatures who will do terrible things to you if you trespass on their land. There are sorcerers capable of manipulating the fabric of reality, and ancient relics capable of toppling nations.<br /> <br /> It's all real with tangible evidence of its existence. So would humanity actually have incentive to explore the hard sciences?<br /> <br /> Would they even have been allowed to do so in the first place? Given how some of these pantheon leaders never wanted humanity to grow as powerful as it has?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-03-2017, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T08:49:38-07:00","id":1124315,"title":"","content":"I would say that there would be a different but equally compelling reason to look to the hard sciences, if there are actual trolls eating your children and centaurs carrying off women wouldn't you seek better way to protect yourself than &quot;Hope a scion shows up&quot;? Chemists would have evolved from Alchemists rather than replacing them. And I recall Neil flat out saying even pre-visitation Scions with a more mental or social bent can introduce massive paradigm shifts into technology and culture. It seems like it provides a reasonable set of options for a different course to a recognizable if distinct societal, political, and philosophical landscape to what we have.<br /> <br /> I'm not super well versed on all ten of the core pantheons, but seems to me that it is mostly the theoi that would object to humans gaining power just because they're gaining power, and even then mostly the first generation, the rest probably wouldn't be apocolypically upset as long as they continued to pay respect where it was due or maintained spiritual clarity. The Netjer and Teotl mostly seem to just want existence to keep chugging along so as long as none of these changes upset that as a group they'd probably stick to wary glances. The Shen and Kami seem more about order so as long as that's maintained I can see them letting things slide a little, from what I gather those two culture strike a weird sort of hybrid of hide-bound tradition and cutting edge modern ideas even without visibly active gods. As long as Odin gets his warriors and hanged men I doubt he gives a flip. It seems like most of the largest problems can be covered by either innovator X being a scion or god Y protecting them from god Z.<br /> <br /> *Shrug* But Yeah, I think it's mostly on the individual groups to draw the exact lines. I think your points are spot on if we keep to the real myths, it's when you throw everything into the mix at once that the waters get muddied. I hate that I mostly keep going to the Greeks for examples but, would Zeus have been such a womanizer if he had to worry about Hera and Isis having a night out and the later inspiring the former by mentioning how jealousy free life has been since Osiris lost his &quot;thing&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T09:56:30-07:00","id":1124342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124315#post1124315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that there would be a different but equally compelling reason to look to the hard sciences, if there are actual trolls eating your children and centaurs carrying off women wouldn't you seek better way to protect yourself than &quot;Hope a scion shows up&quot;? Chemists would have evolved from Alchemists rather than replacing them. And I recall Neil flat out saying even pre-visitation Scions with a more mental or social bent can introduce massive paradigm shifts into technology and culture. It seems like it provides a reasonable set of options for a different course to a recognizable if distinct societal, political, and philosophical landscape to what we have.<br /> <br /> I'm not super well versed on all ten of the core pantheons, but seems to me that it is mostly the theoi that would object to humans gaining power just because they're gaining power, and even then mostly the first generation, the rest probably wouldn't be apocolypically upset as long as they continued to pay respect where it was due or maintained spiritual clarity. The Netjer and Teotl mostly seem to just want existence to keep chugging along so as long as none of these changes upset that as a group they'd probably stick to wary glances. The Shen and Kami seem more about order so as long as that's maintained I can see them letting things slide a little, from what I gather those two culture strike a weird sort of hybrid of hide-bound tradition and cutting edge modern ideas even without visibly active gods. As long as Odin gets his warriors and hanged men I doubt he gives a flip. It seems like most of the largest problems can be covered by either innovator X being a scion or god Y protecting them from god Z.<br /> <br /> *Shrug* But Yeah, I think it's mostly on the individual groups to draw the exact lines. I think your points are spot on if we keep to the real myths, it's when you throw everything into the mix at once that the waters get muddied. I hate that I mostly keep going to the Greeks for examples but, would Zeus have been such a womanizer if he had to worry about Hera and Isis having a night out and the later inspiring the former by mentioning how jealousy free life has been since Osiris lost his &quot;thing&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Chinese pantheon, I can see being alright with the advancement of science, given their focus on transmutation and progress. But I was under the impression the Kami were nature spirits and shied away from major developmental progress in favor of a more patient, traditionalist approach.<br /> <br /> I don't know much of anything about the Persian deities, but I think they created mortals specifically to be their slaves. If I'm wrong about that, somebody correct me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The Teotl would be potentially ruined by the advancement of scientific exploration. Once mortals discovered the rising of the sun was the result of the earth's rotation, and not because sacrificing your daughter on a stone slab gave your god the strength to lift it into the sky. I imagine the Aztecs would be mighty pissed after finding that out.<br /> <br /> The Norse pantheon would probably be okay with it, they didn't really like magic to begin with. Which, by the way, I would love a shard which features the Norse cultists inventing technology to travel between dimensions via the Nine Realms.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Pesedjet seem to be all about strict order and rigid hierarchy. If the mythology is to be believed, the entire pharaoh line consisted of Scions, meaning your society was governed by a demigod, rather than mortal men and women. I don't know how they'd feel about deviating from the norm in such a fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:46:41-07:00","id":1124374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124184#post1124184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for clarifying. I was watching a video on most dangerous places to visit and one of them depicted people washing idols and letting their children swim in the river, so I wasn't sure if that was still a major thing or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> But on that note, I've been watching educational videos about some of this stuff and discovered that some of the old pantheons such as the Norse and Pesedjet actually did have human characteristics. Namely, their deities were subject to disease, age and physical injury. When one or more gods became unfit to do their jobs, they passed their station onto somebody more qualified. Which is how I like to imagine modernization happened over the ages in the Scion setting. Some pantheons would adapt better than others, given the nature of how their pantheons and cultures work.<br /> <br /> The Greeks, for example, are among some of the most egocentric, megalomaniac ass holes in all the mythology I've come across. If you're not a god, they don't care about your opinion. If you are a god, they don't care unless you're more popular than them. If you're more popular than them, they will challenge you in front of everybody to satisfy their insecurities. If you win said challenge, the throw a temper tantrum!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, that's totally still a thing... millions of people still do that... the guy who tried to get a law passed to curb the practice of torture in the name of exorcism got shot and killed in broad daylight (now you know where Sense8 got that storyline), and many so called lower caste people still bathe in the rotted leftovers of Brahmin's meals in order to imbibe some of their vaunted purity... it's just that, millions of people <i>also</i> think all these things are nuts. And those aren't people in some way rebelling against the Gods... they're followers of the Gods who insist that the Gods hate these practices as much as the people do. And they're not new cults (not that the age of a religious movement should in any way invalidate or lower it's inherent value to the world at large) but practices at least hundreds of years old (for some of the personal Bhakti movements) and much much older (like Tantra and Aghori).<br /> <br /> I'm just pointing out that it's not a question of 'do we stay true to the religion and make the Gods assholes, or sugarcoat religion and make them nice' when the religion sugar coated itself eons ago (you know, as far as sugar coating can be said to include naked people covering themselves in ashes and hanging around with skulls in cremation grounds). Both these sides have ancient scriptures and modern adherents to go around, so choice for the ST is literally 'do I want the Gods to be assholes, or not', since religion doesn't come into it (or rather religion has both bases covered).<br /> <br /> Yes, some Pantheons contain asshole members, but not all of them... the Deva ideal is for all their followers to achieve Divinity, the Orisha literally have Innovation as a Virtue, the Shen are constantly evolving and modernizing, the Teotl have been shown to care about the well-being of the World and their people above all else, and the Aesir may think mages have cooties but that didn't stop one from ruling them. So the idea that the World would be some kind of dark age hell because the Gods are undeniably real in the World just doesn't compute for me.<br /> <br /> Also, it's the Mesopotamians who created humans as the slave race, not the Persians IIRC. And Tonatiuh is already aware that Amaterasu Ra and Surya are <i>also</i> the Sun... I think he can deal with people figuring out it's also a mere ball of burning gasses.<br /> <br /> All that being said, I think we've derailed this thread enough... if you'd like to continue this discussion (including the Hindu ideals of perfection of the Gods and how that gets totally messed up when the many varieties of Hinduism can't actually agree on who God is), please feel free to PM me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:38:27-07:00","id":1124766,"title":"","content":"Just to let my opinion be know, I think Gods could adapt and change, but the decision of how much is Storyteller wise. I, particularly, think that if you let all Gods accepting the general today's standards, what is a general massive change of their old ways of think with the reasoning that &quot;they would learn their lessons&quot; or &quot;learn to know better&quot;, seems weird that their other bad behaviours of the Gods would not change too (specially in Loki's case, because it almost always backfires on him), but them you dont have more the same Gods of the myths. In many thousand years they would be different people if they could change, so I think is better to change their outlook but not their nature and behaviour.<br /> <br /> But if in your game wants to have no connections with persecutions and prejudices, keep as the Game certainly will be, clean of it. Is more a matter of what your audience wants and accepts than anything else. Is like in a history film everybody wears clothes that cover their &quot;naughty&quot; bits, when people of that time probably didnt care. It is needed, and preferable, for a modern audience, and is not a problem. But I'm prolonging myself on this digression, and there is other thread entirely for this discussion.<br /> <br /> I dont think it would be some form of Dark Age if there were Gods, but certainly would be very different. The scientific method would be dead before arrival, as people in the Renaissance (would be a renaissance if the classical stuff would be somewhat alive all the time? seem more like a awakening) and in the Enlightenment would have a lot of trouble trying to create a method to analyse the world sceptically and methodically in a world that things happen, and stop happening, by desire of Gods, Demigods, magical creatures and mostly a bunch of other sentient stuff, and for things that might have many different explanations, all real, at the same time (as example, how the sun moves on the sky).<br /> <br /> Science and Technology wise, it would probably be close to the Roman technological development, in a way that engineering would boom faster than science, with different technologies being created more for practical needs. Science would develop more in an Alchemical light, on it mix different beliefs and general ideas of how things behave, and could move closer to the scientific method as repetition and knowledge is spread, but it would never be as it is. I dont think electricity would ever be a thing, but I do think we would have cars in some moment. Also, we probably would never go to the moon or create a space station, as mostly all Gods would consider this a heresy, and, with the exception with a few more crazy Scions, nobody would have the know-how of all that is needed to go there.<br /> <br /> But I dont think the Game, when release, will care for this, and neither will I. It is simply easier (and probably, the only playable option) to ignore the most daring differences that would appear on our history and play on our modern world. About the politics I would consider that most of the big politic changes around the world would have some divine influence, or at least cultist influence, somehow. Not decided by it, but certainly influenced. Like, the French Revolution is against a government that, besides all that they did, also join in some Dyonisiac Parties wasting French Gold, while the revolutionaries would have some influence from the Celtic Gods that would want the power back to the French people. The Gods didnt decide the conflict, it was done by human own merits and flaws, but they certainly direct some stuff and make it more like they desire.<br /> <br /> On Modern World that would be more complicated. Any and all politicians and political parties would have a opinion on Gods, mystical creatures and Pantheons. For example the Democrats could be against the influence of the Theoi, but wanting a bigger integration of mystical creatures on society, while the Republicans would be more in favour of the Theoi influence, with Trump wanting to create a wall keep the Teotl on Mexico. I'm not American and I'm not trying to imply that would be the opinion of any party or politician, I'm just trying to make an example with politicians and parties that more or less everybody knows. If your game is inclined to the political, it would be very interesting to see a game like that, where a politician tries to get votes from the mythological population while another try to rally them against them because of how they bring curses, plagues, destruction, etc. It could be a very good social commentary, if you are inclined in doing so.<br /> <br /> Each country, specially the non-Democratic, like China and North Korea, and the ones with more related Pantheons, like China and Japan, would have different influences over their politics, would have a different approach of how the pantheons influenciate them, as it can get more personal when the Gods literally put some of those governments in place and some of those governor and politicians can be descendants of , and might even become, God's themselves.<br /> <br /> A interesting change, that I'm thinking about while writing it, is to make Greece a country that, traditionally, is always governed by a Scion or God descent of some sort. They could still be a democratic country, but the election would be not only about their plans to Greece, their economic strategy, and their views on pollution and abortion, but also about which God or Hero is he descendent from.<br /> <br /> Also, still on the descendant subject, a lot of celebrities and public persons would claim to have some godlike parentage of some sort, being it true or not. Do you think it could be verified by some sort of blood exam? The Gods, as usual, would not manifest itself about it until it is somewhat damaging to their image, so maybe would be more interesting to have some form of test, maybe to say if someone is a Scion and of which Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Also on the politics topics, how about the Pantheons relations to the Governments? The Shen literally flies over China, while China is an Atheist Communist country. Shouldnt one of them, maybe both, do something about the other? The other pantheons are less political, but wouldnt be good to all Pantheons to have an Ambassador in other countries, to help with politics and bureaucracy? Also would be great to have a Spokesperson, even if it is still a God, someone to work with the press. Maybe even a official twitter account for the Pantheon, like most governments nowadays have. (like Hermes twitting &quot;Zeus woke up today with a headache, so get your umbrellas ready&quot;).<br /> <br /> This is all taking in consideration that the Gods not only does exist, but also everybody knows and accepts that they exist, that I believe is the Scion 2 vibe. By the way, why do the Gods hide? I mean, they can hide and I understand that they hiding sometimes to do stuff that they want without being bothered by mortals, but why doesnt they have an actual seeming to everybody? Why dont they meet with presidents or stuff like that, not disguised or in dreams or some thing like that, I mean scheduling a meeting and going to meet a the White House?<br /> <br /> (Also Also, Would the Gods be somewhat responsible for what their Scions do or their elements do? Could, lets say, Zeus be charged for homicide for hitting someone with a lightning? [I dont think so because, first, you cant prove it was him, other God or even just a regular lightning, and second, he probably have some level of diplomatic immunity]. Does Gods have something like a G20, some form of reunion to discuss inter-pantheon relations and agreements?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:50:15-07:00","id":1124834,"title":"","content":"I've had this thought a lot lately. While it holds true that everyone's going to look at it differently and that's great, that's a big part of the intent, my two cents is basically this: Most of these pantheons can't agree on <i>anything.</i> If they did decide to mess with politics, just how would they agree on what to do or how to do it? That's not to say it doesn't happen, but at some point I figure most of them would make a broad agreement to let mortals mostly decide their own government, and then half of them would break that agreement two seconds later but have to do it with a modicum of subtlety. And what do gods do in this game when they can't act directly? That's where we, the eponymous Scions, come in. <br /> <br /> Obviously this varies from one pantheon to the next. While they all have their own internal relations and usually a feud or three, some are a lot better at unifying and declaring a group position, or at least sticking to their own rules, while others have Virtues that are directly opposed to certain policies. But one thing that set me on this train of thought was when the Shen preview mentioned &quot;...the Taiwanese government over the Chinese Communist government \u2014 a conflict on which the Shen are studiously silent.\u200b&quot; My first thought was <i>Why would the most litigious pantheon not issue a statement on something that important?</i> My second thought was <i>Because there is no possible way the higher-ups all agree on one.</i> Then <i>So are they just doing nothing about it, or being very subtle, or even skirmishing with each other over the whole thing?</i> And so on. <br /> <br /> \u200bApply this thinking to other pantheons less apt to send out a pantheon-wide memo (or read one, for that matter) and it paints something of a picture. Figure most of the gods want to seem united, like they are one body with a common goal and will, but in practice we all know they often want different things. And if there are mortal or mostly-mortal or pseudo-mortal actors not bound by any agreement, politically conscious citizens they just happen to be related to, well, it's only a crime if you're caught (said people who aren't Heru). A god shall not run for prime minister, but a savvy scion of Odin can make a great campaign manager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:06:15-07:00","id":1124907,"title":"","content":"I admit, I dont know a lot about the Shen, I know mostly from Scion and from the Sun Wukong literature, but I dont see any good reason to the Shen be &quot;studiously silent&quot; about it. Why would they be in favour of the Chinese Communist? They are a Atheistic Regime, that is doing work (and a good work, with you believe the last census) on making people do not worship them. (I'm not quite sure how they do that in a world people actually know they are there, but I believe is more on the line of teaching people they are not the creators of the world and they are not so powerful). To be honest, my first thought was more in line of <i> &quot;Oh, they dont want to tackle that political discussion. Moving on.&quot; </i>.<br /> <br /> I know the Gods have many opinions, even inside a single Pantheon, but that dont mean the Pantheon hasn't a opinion and a position, specially considering that the Pantheons dont organize in a Democracy. If Odin had saw the USSR as a threat for anything he cares, he would put the Aesir against it, ordering them if necessary. The Aesir would be against USSR, with a few exceptions. Mostly of the Pantheons have a hierarchy of some sort, so they have organization enough to make their own decision and have a political position. Is not mandatory that they have one, the Aesir could not have a opinion to the USSR as a group, even if each individual has one. What I'm saying is that the Pantheons seem less like actual governments (as it would be, considering that many top Gods are their Pantheons Kings or Emperors), and more as groups, put together through family ties, marriages, people beliefs and geographic origin.<br /> <br /> As far as the game is showing itself, the pantheons are just groupings of Gods, that meddle with the world when please themselves, using Scions as their minions and lackeys (I dont think I saw a reason of why they dont go direct on World to do stuff, but I'm sure there is one), acting as groups only against threats of universal scale. Each God has personality and something to do with their specific kind of connection with something in humanity, but Pantheons doesn't have connections with human groups. The Theoi seem to care the same about Greece, Oklahoma and Rio de Janeiro. They have no tie-ins with the empires that call their names, for the land where they where once the worshipped Gods, or the governments that came after. Are all the Gods so emotionally fatigued for once have had empires built and destroyed on their wishes that they are now just not caring about groups, but as humanity as a whole, disregarding all that past? If in war a country deliberately destroys the remains of a Viking settlement that marked what once where a big temple that honoured the Aesir, does they get a position? Do they start a official war against this army? Even if they cant act directly, can they send an army of Scions to fight? Or are they limited to subtle ways, like just treachery? Or are the Aesir unable to start a war? What can they do them? Can they send sanctions? Or they are limited to use more treachery? Do they even care?<br /> <br /> Of course this is more a personal bother than a game problem. Is simply to argue that &quot;they are families, not governments&quot;, &quot;they care about the whole world, in a humanity scale&quot;, and &quot;they don't meddle with human affairs and governments&quot;. The best reasoning for such is that they agreed on not doing so or are unable, maybe both. You can even say that the Gods have a pact to do so, to avoid wars and such, and no side want to be the one to break it, hence why they use Scions. You can even use this argument and the give positioning to the Pantheons in favour or against political sides, and saying that they cant simple change governments when they please, needing to push and pull strings to do so. But not giving positions to the Pantheons seem... too clean cut. But I like more mature games, with real life problems and complexities, so I'm bias. At this point they could make a new book line mixing the World of Darkness and Scion, where Gods can be much more... unclean, for lack of a better world, and it would find a public. Or a Scion supplement.<br /> <br /> About the Scions being elected, I dont think any government would allow that. Shock of interests and all. Maybe if there is a tradition on that, going from many generations. But a campaign manager I see no problem.<br /> <br /> Trying to answer this thread title, I believe the most official and coherent answer to this question in relation of the basic books is: as Pantheons, they dont. As individual God's, they use Scions and mystical creatures to try to pull and push politics to their preference, be it in favour of reforestation or war.<br /> <br /> But a derivative question from this would be, &quot;How modern countries deal with the Pantheons?&quot;. Do they accept their existence? Do they send or receive ambassadors? Is there some form of relation between them, or are the Gods too distant from mortals to have relations with them? Could Communist China attack the Shen flying heaven that is on their aerial territory? Could they even, bureaucrat speaking, start a war? Does the Pantheons have a UN representation? If not, why not, they seem to meddle (and seem to be know that they meddle) very much in the world? Wouldn't be easier to open official communications with them, to try to ease tensions or maybe ask for commercial or political benefits?<br /> <br /> I think my first chronicle of Scion 2 will be a political one.<br /> <br /> (Just before someone comments, I dont think that you cant tackle real life problems with Scion as it is, is just that they are, as a default matter, cleaning the game from more risqu\u00e9 topics, limiting many &quot;real life problems&quot; that could arrive from this scenario)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:51:55-07:00","id":1124928,"title":"","content":"I don't think the gods would have a presence in the UN, or any &quot;official&quot; position in world government. Just a few exerts from the April Preview.<br /> <br /> &quot;Heroic Expectations<br /> Beneath silent respect, fawning worship and fear, mortals hold Heroes to an implied duty:<br /> Protect us, and act as our representative among divine and legendary powers . Heroes<br /> bind, tame them or slay monsters. They plead the people\u2019s case before angry Gods, or tell<br /> mortals what the Gods want. They explain why children vanish on the full moon by the<br /> ancient mounds, and if they can\u2019t convince the beings inside to give the kids back, they<br /> can at least tell mortals how to prevent it from happening again. Sometimes holy<br /> covenants spell these expectations out, but most of the time people expect Heroes to do it<br /> because of who they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;How could you not believe? Gods walk among us. If you belong to a cult, you\u2019ve probably seen<br /> one of the Scions, or gazed upon their magic. Perhaps it happened once in your life. One of the<br /> sons of Zeus came to bless your modest temple, or an Orixa manifested in full glory at the apex<br /> of a ceremony. You\u2019ve seen. You believe.<br /> It\u2019s difficult to say if this is sentiment is shared by the global majority regarding their own<br /> pantheons, by a significant minority, or by a smaller sliver of the World\u2019s population.<br /> Contemporary tradition makes divine worship a private affair, and not everyone gathers in a cult.<br /> Many families hand down a few idols and prayers, keeping their faith while staying disconnected<br /> from the larger community. Some cults have long since stopped worshiping with any real<br /> sincerity, and are indistinguishable from sports clubs or secular charities save for a statue or<br /> some bit of nonsense (sometimes far corrupted from the original Ancient Egyptian, sometimes<br /> not) that you\u2019ve got to mutter to join. It\u2019s practically impossible to take a census of the total<br /> number of faithful cults, and probably undesirable, because it would weaken the network of<br /> customs that let Gods and modern mortals coexist in relative peace.&quot;<br /> <br /> From both of these we can gather that the gods are around but most governments probably just keep Scions or at least Priests on speed dial in case the need to get a message to Olympus quickly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:25:54-07:00","id":1124943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124766#post1124766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to let my opinion be know, I think Gods could adapt and change, but the decision of how much is Storyteller wise. I, particularly, think that if you let all Gods accepting the general today's standards, what is a general massive change of their old ways of think with the reasoning that &quot;they would learn their lessons&quot; or &quot;learn to know better&quot;, seems weird that their other bad behaviours of the Gods would not change too (specially in Loki's case, because it almost always backfires on him), but them you dont have more the same Gods of the myths. In many thousand years they would be different people if they could change, so I think is better to change their outlook but not their nature and behaviour.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One big reason for why they might not have changed in 2E has already been pointed out earlier in the thread. The fact that Fate conspires to guide them along an appointed course in line with their past behavior. The jerk gods had been jerk gods for hundreds / thousands of years and were widely established as such in the minds of mortal society. Even if they did want to change at some point, it would be nigh impossible for them to do so. You said yourself that Loki's tried to change, but it always backfires on him.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit confused as to how you can change your outlook, but not your personality or behavior. If you see things from a different perspective, but continue to act in contradiction to that perspective, it results in depression and self loathing. That's a dangerous mindset for mortals, much less the creators of the multiverse. I don't think any of us want to see what it looks like when a god lashes out as part of a desperate cry for help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oh, also, Titans are a thing! Did we forget about that?<br /> <br /> You know, the very embodiments of nature itself, who couldn't give 1/4th of a rat's ass about human ideology?<br /> <br /> The Titans who, in second edition, are still roaming about the land because the Titanomachy is less black and white than it was in 1E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-04-2017, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T17:03:08-07:00","id":1125004,"title":"","content":"Titans aren't necessarily embodiments of nature in 2e, that's the territory of primordials, and even some of them interact with humanity. Not saying Some titans aren't apathetic forces of nature of course, just that a lot of them are more or less gods who have a different title. Fomorians, Asuras, Jotnar, Titanes; sure, some embody forces of nature, but most interact with gods on the same level and a lot even interact with humans just as the gods do. And we know some of them are allied with their pantheons and have had hints that some might have scions themselves.<br /> <br /> And yeah, people have already beat me to the punch, but I was going to point out that its pretty hard for one pantheon to make any sweeping changes in a universe where every pantheon is real and getting in each other's business. The world might exist the way it does because of inter-pantheon conflict. Of course, if someone wants to spend the time and research to create an alternate history timeline, then more power to you! But if you don't wanna go that route, then there are plenty of options for why the world would still be as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:55:20-07:00","id":1125278,"title":"","content":"Maybe I expressed myself bad when I said outlook, but I mean it not in how they see the world but as how they interact in it. Ares, as God of War, now uses machine guns and AK-47 and use bulletproof vests. Hermes now uses Internet. Anubis wears suits on cemeteries. They change their outside look, and the way they interact and experience their relation with the World (some, not all of course) but keep being the same people, with the same functions, personalities, quirks, interests, merits and flaws. Just updating some of them to a modern scenario, is what I meant.<br /> <br /> The Fate forcing would help to maintain it in their places, but not stopping them to change. If Hera divorced from Zeus, certainly the Fate would try to conspire to push her back into place, in form of her seeing how it affect matrimonies and friends and families asking her to return, and awkward unsuspected meetings with Zeus in romantic fashion, but she could still push herself to get out of the mold, and the more she kept herself out, and the more people would accept it, the less the Fate would try to force her. When she find her place in Legend (maybe as goddess of Divorce, or a Goddess of the Modern Women) the Fate would them try to fix her on where she is. Same happened with Ares to Mars. (By the way, I mean that what backfires on Loki is not him trying to change his Fate, but many of his pranks and plans). It is more a question of how their change fit in the Fates Narrative (and Fate seems to love those) and how much determination the Gods put into it, what many of them are made of it.<br /> <br /> And why the hell wouldnt the Gods have a depression after centuries being the same person, and noticing that they can't change? Can you imagine a God, trying and trying, time and time again, being someone different, doing something to feel better about himself and his unending life, but seeing himself push back again by the inescapable chains of Fate, that demands that you play your part, and only your part, in the cosmic play? This is depression folder if I ever saw one. (I'm thinking in Hephaestus trying to divorce from Aphrodite, but any time he tries, the Fate cant let him forget and move on, and he always comes back crying in a Nectar induced drunkenness to his ever unfaithful). If they cant escape that or they live in this miserable pointless life, or they live in a deep denial of it, or they embrace their own willing-less destinies as puppets.<br /> <br /> My point is that, after 2000 (or more) of time since the original legends that put the Fate in place, some would be different. The wouldnt start to change only after thousand of years, maybe just a few centuries (or less), but I see no reason why they would wait thousands of years. In this universe that Gods are real, and do interact with people in a reasonable basis, their legends wouldn't be thousand years would, there would be some new legend every half century or so. Their mythologies would expand as they act and react between themselves and humanity. There would have been other Trojan Wars, other Vedas, other Edas. Other Scions would be members of Pantheons, representing different concepts, like Esculapio became the God of medicine, there would be a God of Alchemy, a God of Horse Races, a God of the Sea Travel.<br /> <br /> I know it is impossible that the creators to create a system like that, and I will be more or less ignoring most of my own criticism when I play it because it would be nigh impossible to really create this world, a world where Gods are real and changing people. And more important, playing with a vastly different set of Gods wouldn't be nearly as fun.<br /> <br /> Just transporting them from the past in a new fashion, moral code and habits in the modern setting in a world they were suppose to be a part of basically every major event in our history (and many, many minor) seems... too easy. But is mostly what I gonna do when I play (with a few changes here and there. I still gonna make they more politically influential, turning the Pantheons in political Powers in the world, for example). I'm just pointing what I see as weird inconsistencies and trying to come with variations to see what people think and for those who want to try them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8375\" data-vbnamecard=\"8375\">vonpenguin</a>, I haven't seem those excerpts before, but even if the Gods have no direct connection to the little people, and to many of his cult that practice in a different and insincere way, why can't they have a direct representation on Earth? I dont remember seeing why Gods cant just walk on the streets as themselves (in 1e was that fate would basically try to make they act like Gods, sending challenges and other problems), or meet with presidents in official offices or something, but even considering they cant because of the same reason (or a similar) in 1e, why can't they have a spokesperson serving as their official voice, like an Ambassador? They can't speak for every god, but would serve as the general spokesman for the each Pantheon. (&quot;About the attacks of the 3 giant 3 headed dogs in the streets of Philadelphia, the Theoi official Spokesperson claimed that they have no connection to the guardian of the Underworld known as Cerberus, but that the Theoi are sending a team of heroes, investigators and analysts to work with the local professionals.&quot;). Besides all that people would still have smaller cults, very different of one another, and wouldnt act as a single singular religion (as the would not be a spiritual guide, just a spokesperson) and every god still can act as they want, secretively or not.<br /> <br /> In a multi-pantheon world, they could mess around on their own lands and peoples, as they originally did, so problems only would arrive in conflicts of territory, which in the past has seem to be resolved not by God-Wars, but by human-wars. So, if they agreed very earlier (and I mean, very very early) that there wouldnt be God-Wars, but all conflicts would be solved by human wars with only indirect help of the Gods, that basically means that Gods are playing a world-sized game of War, which (as mostly game of Wars I played) they loose interest after a while and are now just seeing how things are going, making a personal interference here and there as each individual God sees fit to himself and fighting their usual People-Squishing City-Wrecking Civilizations-Destroyers World-Eating Enemies. That seems like the best explanation so far. A bunch of Gods dont like it, but is impossible to please all of those guys. (Still dont explain why they wouldnt change, but it isnt here nor there).<br /> <br /> Does someone know the official reason, from a Excerpt or Ask Neall Thread, about why can't Gods affect politics directly and officially, by official ambassadors or in person?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T12:39:28-07:00","id":1125311,"title":"","content":"Well the ambassadors are Scions, and if a god felt strongly enough I'm sure they would have a socially inclined Scion take the job. It just seems to not be super important to most I guess. Especially in modern day Democracies where leaders typically only last a handful of years I imagine most gods rather work on the subject of their interest without the silly mortal middlemen. <br /> <br /> The Exert is from the April preview, the one with the Satyr callings and the Flame and Forge stuff in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T16:44:27-07:00","id":1125412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1125311#post1125311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Exert is from the April preview, the one with the Satyr callings and the Flame and Forge stuff in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's a Satyr calling?<br /> <br /> I am intrigued!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T17:19:26-07:00","id":1125420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1125412#post1125412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> There's a Satyr calling?<br /> <br /> I am intrigued!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to disappoint, but it's technically a Satyr <i>Path</i> ... there's no Satyr Calling (that we know of) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:52:03-07:00","id":1141195,"title":"","content":"So, I recently came across some of this...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Historical Vikings</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S8kRmidhlTE\" data-code=\"S8kRmidhlTE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/S8kRmidhlTE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Historical Samurai</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oJqbh-tjJVE\" data-code=\"oJqbh-tjJVE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/oJqbh-tjJVE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Historical Persians</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=naPUYTKEMc8\" data-code=\"naPUYTKEMc8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/naPUYTKEMc8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T14:45:22-07:00","id":1141216,"title":"","content":"To be fair on the last one, a bunch of slave owners proudly proclaiming their own liberty while vilifying their opponents as having &quot;slave armies&quot; because they recruited FREED slaves.... is kind of quintessentially American. We did it against Britain in the War for Independence, and the War of 1812; Texas did it against Mexico, and the Confederates did it against the Union.<br /> <br /> I don't find it implausible that Sparta used such hypocritical propaganda against Persia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-17-2017, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T16:05:17-07:00","id":1146181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1124113#post1124113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It works like this: when you do something shitty, people remember. They'll expect you to do something shitty in the future. When a god does something shitty, they suddenly find themselves in a lot of situations where they are expected - inclined and encouraged, even - to act exactly the same way.<br /> <br /> Zeus has a wandering eye and fights with his wife all the time, even though he loves her. Fate conspires to put a lot of women in his path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any way for Zeus or any other god to change that? or at least ask Fate to lock them in new behaviours instead of old ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T05:18:05-07:00","id":1146299,"title":"","content":"My guess would be it is like anyone trying to change a shitty habit of theirs but complicated by the fact the World itself is conspiring to provide temptation and opportunity. The way to change is simply stop engaging in behaviors till the habit is broken or you at least get used to saying no to bait. Gods and likely more powerful scions find that complicated by fate directly. An alcoholic who is literally finding themselves with booze veritably thrown at them when they try to stop drinking or a serial adulterer trying to go straight finds a constant series of sexy young co-eds mysteriously losing their clothing and inhibitions in their general vicinity. Like when a character tries to go straight in a comedy where the universe is dumping on them except exactly that. But with maybe a bit more gravitas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","user":"Alpharius","date":". 10-03-2017, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T12:57:22-07:00","id":1146418,"title":"","content":"I wonder which deities would be in favor of Transhumanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T15:03:22-07:00","id":1146453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1123877-how-do-the-various-pantheons-influence-modern-politics?p=1146418#post1146418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder which deities would be in favor of Transhumanism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Many tricksters, I would imagine. Transhumanism is part of their job! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-03-2017, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}